      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "If using dried beans, soak overnight in cold water."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat oil in a large saucepan. Gently fry lardons, chorizo, and sausage for 5 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add onion and garlic. Cook for 5 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add beans, bay leaves, saffron, and smoked paprika."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pour in stock to just cover everything."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Bring to a gentle simmer. Skim any foam from the surface. Cook on low heat for 1.5 to 2 hours, stirring occasionally, until beans are very soft and broth is thick."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Remove onion quarters and bay leaves. Slice sausages and return to the pot."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Season. Serve in deep bowls."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Beans falling apart",
              "cause": "Cooked at too high a simmer",
              "fix": "Keep heat very gentle. Fabada should just barely bubble."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Broth too thin",
              "cause": "Too much liquid",
              "fix": "Mash a few beans into the broth to thicken it naturally."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Too salty",
              "cause": "Cured meats and stock added too much salt together",
              "fix": "Use low-salt stock and taste before adding any extra salt."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Fabada asturiana is to Asturias what cassoulet is to the Languedoc: a bean and meat stew that defines a region. Asturias is a cool, green, mountainous region in northern Spain, and the dish reflects its climate. The original recipe uses three specific cured meats called the compangu: chorizo, morcilla, and lacon. It is eaten for lunch, never dinner, and is considered too heavy for summer. Tinned fabada is sold across Spain as one of the most respected convenience foods."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
